<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Export options for an App Store / TestFlight build.

    NO SECRETS ARE IN THIS FILE, and none may be added to it. No team ID, no
    certificate, no provisioning-profile name, no Apple ID, no App Store Connect
    API key. The team is supplied on the command line at export time so that a
    developer's account identity never becomes a committed fact:

        xcodebuild -exportArchive \
            -archivePath  build/TruePad.xcarchive \
            -exportPath   build/export \
            -exportOptionsPlist ios/TruePadApp/ExportOptions.plist \
            -allowProvisioningUpdates \
            DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=YOUR_TEAM_ID

    NOTHING HERE HAS BEEN RUN SUCCESSFULLY. Producing a signed archive needs an
    Apple Developer team, which this repository deliberately does not carry, so
    this file is a prepared path rather than a demonstrated one. See
    docs/APP-STORE-READINESS.md for what that boundary means and what is still
    owed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>method</key>
    <string>app-store-connect</string>

    <!-- Let Xcode fetch/refresh what it needs rather than pinning a profile by
         name, which would bind this file to one developer's account. -->
    <key>signingStyle</key>
    <string>automatic</string>

    <!-- TruePad performs no network I/O, so there are no symbols worth uploading
         for crash symbolication of a network path; but dSYM upload is what makes
         any future crash report readable at all, and costs nothing. -->
    <key>uploadSymbols</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- App thinning is irrelevant here: one architecture, no asset variants. -->
    <key>thinning</key>
    <string>&lt;none&gt;</string>

    <!-- Bitcode has been removed from the toolchain; stated explicitly so nobody
         re-adds it believing it is required. -->
    <key>compileBitcode</key>
    <false/>

    <!-- Do NOT let the export step invent an export-compliance answer. The
         truthful declaration lives in the app's Info.plist
         (ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption = true) and the determination is still
         open — see docs/EXPORT-DETERMINATION-PACKET.md. -->
    <key>manageAppVersionAndBuildNumber</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
